.TH PACKAGE-CLEANER 1 "October 2026" "Package Cleaner @VERSION@"
.SH NAME
package-cleaner \- review and explicitly remove unnecessary software
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B package-cleaner
.RI [ options ] " [command]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reviews APT and Flatpak applications. Without arguments, opens the guided
terminal menu. Discovery and previews do not authorize removal.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help
Display all supported commands and options.
.TP
.B --enable-removal
Offer execution after validation and a separate explicit confirmation.
.TP
.B gui
Open the graphical interface, which uses its own final confirmation dialog.
.SH SAFETY
Run as your normal user. The existing privileged helper requests administrator
authorization only for APT execution. Removal can run package-manager scripts;
previews cannot guarantee absolute safety. Back up important data first.
.SH FILES
Preferences and queue data use XDG configuration and state directories.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR package-cleaner-gui (1)
